From 675a83e47cf11fd3f3ec3bb9743cb4f6e70d975c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g <g@magnetic.sh>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:27:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm3: run Reflection Beam-1.0-501B-A23B (GGUF) on maya-mm3

Beam is a 501B MoE (256 experts, 8 active, ~23B) whose attention is a
hybrid of 9 global NoPE layers and 43 sliding-window (512) RoPE layers,
each output gated per head, with sandwich norms, a depth-scaled residual,
a group-limited sigmoid router and a logit softcap. It runs on maya-mm3's
placement and expert tiers; a pack with model_type beam switches on:

- Geo::read_beam (mm3_geo.hpp) and the Beam kernels (mm3_kernels.cu):
  GQA attention over a causal key range with an optional window, the
  sliding layers' K/V in a ring of window + chunk rows, BF16/INT8/FP8
  caches and split-K decode; the gate, NoPE query scale, residual,
  plain SwiGLU, group-limited router and softcap
- beam_front / beam_layer (mm3_model.cu): one front for the token,
  window and prompt paths; the experts through each path's own code,
  their output through moe_out (MiniMax: h += y, unchanged)
- plain SwiGLU for the GGUF experts on the GPU and the CPU lane
- Model::eos_ids: <|return|> and <|call|>; INFO model= from the pack
- tools/mm3/pack_beam_gguf.py (llama.cpp's beam GGUFs: unsloth's,
  bartowski's) and tools/mm3/beam_setup.py (the server config)
- the qwen2 pre-tokenizer with NFC (Beam's tokenizer.json)
- serve: Beam's harmony_xml template (its {% generation %} blocks, a
  tool result named after its call) and BeamRewriter for its channels
  and <rfl:parameter> tool calls; <|return|> / <|call|> end a turn
- tests/mm3_beam_test.cu (kernels vs F64 references, needs a GPU) and
  serve/test_beam_frontend.py; docs/BEAM.md; LICENSE.beam (Apache-2.0,
  the bundled chat template)

Not yet run on a GPU: see docs/BEAM.md for what was checked and the
first steps on one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
